# Conventions

## Naming

- **React components:** PascalCase exports (`Dashboard`, `UserCard`), file names kebab-case (`dashboard.tsx`)
- **Hooks:** camelCase with `use` prefix, file names kebab-case (`use-current-user.ts`)
- **Route segments:** kebab-case folders under `app/` (`app/auth/callback/`)
- **Non-component modules:** kebab-case (`auth-session-service.ts`, `query-keys.ts`)
- **Service classes:** PascalCase (`AuthSessionService`); singleton export camelCase (`authSessionService`)
- **Types / interfaces:** PascalCase for exported shapes (`User`, `Bloom`, `Integration`)

## Logic & patterns

- **Server Components by default.** Add `"use client"` only for interactivity, browser APIs, or client-only libraries (TanStack Query hooks).
- **Colocate** feature-specific components and helpers under `features/<name>/` when they are not route-only.
- **Shared primitives** live in `components/ui/` or `components/` at the repo root — avoid deep cross-imports between unrelated features.
- **Services as classes with singleton export.** Methods are async and return plain data. Construct dependencies (SDK clients) in the constructor.
- **Hooks call services, never SDKs directly.** Components call hooks, never services directly.

## Placement

- **Routes & layouts** → `app/` (thin: compose UI, wire loaders/actions)
- **Route Handlers** → `app/api/<route>/route.ts` (validate input, delegate to feature services)
- **Feature UI + hooks** → `features/<domain>/components`, `features/<domain>/hooks`
- **Feature services** → `features/<domain>/services` (class + singleton)
- **Shared UI** → `components/`
- **Pure helpers** (no React, no env-specific side effects) → `lib/utils/` or `lib/tokens/` etc.
- **Appwrite SDK** → only in `lib/appwrite/client.ts` (browser) and `lib/appwrite/server.ts` (Route Handlers)
